From 94cffc24430151ab9911915256bb7284a3c485e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitri <dms202575p@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 07:11:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Run in Knox Secure Folder / secondary Android users
 (experimental)

The rootfs, box64, Wine and graphics drivers are built with the absolute
prefix /data/data/com.winlator/files/rootfs (ELF interpreter, RUNPATH,
ld.so paths, wineserver dir, X11/Vortek sockets, fontconfig, ALSA).
/data/data is user 0 only, so in Knox (user 150) box64 cannot even exec.

- RootFSRelocator rewrites that prefix in place (same length) to
  /proc/self/fd/9//./././././././././. on extraction, plus a one-time pass
  over an existing rootfs (skips /home and /tmp).
- Guest programs start via sh with fd 9 open on this user's rootfs dir
  (exec "$@" 9<dir: keeps the pid and the fd for every child process).
- Native cache dir from WINLATOR_APP_CACHE_DIR (set from getCacheDir()).
- E: drive path /data/data/com.winlator/storage mapped to /data/user/<id>.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018cLUKUNDhFWb9gSFtJ7vW4
